# T5.4 case 3: a hundred kilobyte cell in the grid. The value is cut to the
# column with an `…` and never formatted whole, so moving the cell cursor
# over it costs what any other row costs — which is what the `draw_ms` budget
# scripts/qa/query-workflow.sh reads off the trace holds it to.
#
# bench.big_text is three rows: a short body, a NULL and the 102,400
# character one. Same statement on both backends.

key c
wait busy
expect ●

key Tab
type select id, body from bench.big_text order by id
key Ctrl-R
wait busy
expect 3 rows

key Shift-Tab
key Shift-Tab
key l
expect Lorem ipsu
expect …
frame big-cell

# Up and down the whole set, twice over, every key its own frame.
key j
key j
key j
key k
key k
key k
key j
key j
key k
key j
key k
key k
frame big-cell-scrolled
key Ctrl-Q
